5d6|n|A quadruped of the genus Equus (E. asinus), smaller than the horse, and having a peculiarly harsh bray and long ears. The tame or domestic ass is patient, slow, and sure-footed, and has become the type of obstinacy and stupidity. There are several species of wild asses which are swift-footed. ; A dull, heavy, stupid fellow; a dolt.	a:17zq,97,5~17zq,97,5	v:17zq,84,2;21vh,68,4~21vh,68,4;17zq,84,2	V:1iek,17,1~1iek,17,1	n:17zq,90,3~17zq,90,3	N:1iek,17,1~1iek,17,1
